The noise model underlying spin qubits is strongly biased toward $Z$ errors, which are far more prevalent than $X$ errors. To illustrate this, we first perform a memory experiment (i.e., storing a single logical qubit over several QEC rounds) under a fixed choice of noise parameters\footnote{For this initial experiment we set $T_{\phi}^\texttt{Store} = T_{\phi}^\texttt{Bus} = 100 \mu\text{s}$ and $T_{\phi}^\texttt{Op} = 30 \mu\text{s}$, deferring a full parameter sweep to later sections.}.

